WEBVTT

00:00.310 --> 00:03.040
June, Nankatsu Middle School

00:00.780 --> 00:05.400
Hooray! Hooray! Nankatsu!

00:06.010 --> 00:08.870
<i>Nankatsu Public Middle School.</i>

00:08.870 --> 00:11.900
<i>Not long ago, it was a fairly common high school,</i>

00:11.900 --> 00:17.320
<i>but now, the passionate gazes of the
youth football association all rest upon it.</i>

00:18.200 --> 00:24.040
<i>Tsubasa became the ace of the football club as soon as he entered Nankatsu Middle School,</i>

00:24.040 --> 00:31.250
<i>winning the National Tournament Championship title two years in a row, together with his old friends from Nankatsu SC.</i>

00:31.250 --> 00:36.300
<i>Now, he faces his last summer as a middle schooler.</i>

00:37.350 --> 00:38.230
Crap!

00:38.230 --> 00:39.720
You idiot! What are you doing?!

00:39.720 --> 00:42.300
Ishizaki, you handle the marking on the other side!

00:42.300 --> 00:45.060
Aw, it was going to be fun...

00:45.060 --> 00:49.310
Sign: Sugimoto Hisami

00:45.060 --> 00:49.310
Tsubasa, you can leave all the defense stuff to Ishizaki.

00:49.310 --> 00:50.440
Hey, you over there!

00:50.440 --> 00:51.940
I can hear you, first grader!

00:51.940 --> 00:52.850
Woopsie.

00:52.850 --> 00:54.380
That wouldn't be good.

00:54.380 --> 00:55.700
Huh?

00:55.700 --> 01:00.740
Tsubasa isn't a forward anymore.
He's a midfielder, unlike before.

01:00.740 --> 01:01.910
Ugh, so?

01:01.910 --> 01:03.910
Sign: Nishimoto Yukari

01:01.910 --> 01:04.840
You really know nothing, don't you?

01:04.840 --> 01:07.170
Wha– that hurts, Yukari...

01:07.170 --> 01:09.730
Well, the midfielders are the core of the team.

01:09.730 --> 01:12.460
The position serves as the team's control tower.

01:12.460 --> 01:17.720
That's why they need to perform well, not only on the offensive side, but also on defense, among other things.

01:17.720 --> 01:19.550
That's how hard it is but...

01:19.550 --> 01:23.760
In my opinion, it's the most suitable position
for Tsubasa, our captain.

01:26.140 --> 01:28.420
Go for it, Tsubasa!

01:28.190 --> 01:30.770
Football Club Coach
Takeshi Furuoya

01:28.420 --> 01:30.770
Go, go! Score that goal!

01:37.400 --> 01:39.030
NANKATSU VS. KIDA

01:39.030 --> 01:42.280
Nankatsu Middle School is just as strong as we expected.

01:42.280 --> 01:45.120
But we'll be representing Shizuoka Prefecture this year!

01:45.120 --> 01:50.580
Us four will shut their offense down like it was nothing!

01:50.580 --> 01:56.660
And the one scoring the victorious goal will be you, Nitta!

01:56.660 --> 01:58.460
I am well aware.

01:58.460 --> 02:00.680
I can score once or twice, if you'd like!

02:01.360 --> 02:09.070
After all, I'm the one who carried Nankatsu SC to the championship in your absence.

02:12.270 --> 02:14.980
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

02:12.270 --> 02:14.980
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

02:15.900 --> 02:18.570
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

02:15.900 --> 02:18.570
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

02:19.490 --> 02:22.200
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

02:19.490 --> 02:22.200
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

02:29.070 --> 02:31.920
<i>moeru you ni hitori demo</i>

02:29.070 --> 02:31.920
<i>I keep running, lying to myself</i>

02:31.920 --> 02:38.170
<i>ikiteyukeru to usobuite hashiritsudzukete</i>

02:31.920 --> 02:38.170
<i>that I can live alone, though the loneliness makes me burn</i>

02:38.170 --> 02:44.050
<i>unobore no morosa wo kimi wa shitteta na no ni</i>

02:38.170 --> 02:44.050
<i>You knew how fragile my self-conceit makes me</i>

02:44.050 --> 02:50.640
<i>kokoro made uchinomaresareta kono yoru ni</i>

02:44.050 --> 02:50.640
<i>In this night that even shattered my heart</i>

02:50.640 --> 02:54.650
<i>kimi no koe sagasu</i>

02:50.640 --> 02:54.650
<i>I hate how weak I am</i>

02:54.650 --> 02:59.150
<i>kono yowasa ga nikui yo</i>

02:54.650 --> 02:59.150
<i>yearning for your voice</i>

02:59.150 --> 03:04.700
<i>ima sugu torimodoshi ni ikanakya</i>

02:59.150 --> 03:04.700
<i>"I've got to get you back right now!"</i>

03:04.700 --> 03:06.280
<i>baka darou?</i>

03:04.700 --> 03:06.280
<i>I'm stupid, right?</i>

03:06.280 --> 03:07.490
<i>ai</i>

03:06.280 --> 03:07.490
<i>Love!</i>

03:07.490 --> 03:11.120
<i>kizudarake no ai wo shinjite</i>

03:07.490 --> 03:11.120
<i>Believing in my scarred love</i>

03:11.120 --> 03:20.880
<i>nagareochita namida sae mo tsuyosa e to kaete</i>

03:11.120 --> 03:20.880
<i>I will turn these shedded tears into strength</i>

03:20.880 --> 03:21.720
<i>ai</i>

03:20.880 --> 03:21.720
<i>Love!</i>

03:21.720 --> 03:25.510
<i>kizudarake no ai da to shite mo</i>

03:21.720 --> 03:25.510
<i>Even though it is a scarred love</i>

03:25.510 --> 03:29.520
<i>bokura no sekai wo tomoshiteru</i>

03:25.510 --> 03:29.520
<i>it lightens up our world</i>

03:29.520 --> 03:35.770
<i>kono ai mo ichido taritomo</i>

03:29.520 --> 03:35.770
<i>I will not let go of this love</i>

03:35.770 --> 03:38.560
<i>hanasanai</i>

03:35.770 --> 03:38.560
<i>for a single moment!</i>

03:40.530 --> 03:45.530
<b><b>EPISODE 29:
START OF SUMMER!</b></b>

03:41.020 --> 03:45.400
Tsubasa Ozora, this was a brilliant performance, not unlike any of your others so far!

03:45.400 --> 03:47.230
Thank you very much!

03:45.710 --> 03:48.240
So even Soccer Eleven is here for interviews?

03:47.230 --> 03:48.590
Tell us about the match!

03:48.240 --> 03:51.070
He's as popular as always!

03:48.590 --> 03:50.000
Let's see...

03:51.070 --> 03:52.670
Well, of course he is.

03:52.670 --> 03:56.250
He was already participating in
High School tryouts during the spring.

03:56.250 --> 04:00.050
He's left us in the dust for the past 3 years.

04:00.050 --> 04:00.960
Yeah.

04:00.960 --> 04:02.460
What are you all talking about?

04:02.460 --> 04:05.470
Isn't football played with 11 players?

04:05.470 --> 04:08.080
His strength is also yours.

04:08.080 --> 04:11.430
Tsubasa hasn't changed, but you've definitely changed a lot!

04:11.520 --> 04:15.580
To think that boss of the Nankatsu Cheer Squad
would become such a lady

04:15.580 --> 04:18.210
right as she becomes a middle schooler...

04:18.210 --> 04:21.280
It sure was a surprise for us Nankatsu veterans, too!

04:21.280 --> 04:22.970
Is that true?

04:22.970 --> 04:25.080
Sanae, the boss of cheerleading squad?!

04:25.080 --> 04:26.240
How unexpected!

04:26.240 --> 04:28.320
She's a totally different person, now.

04:28.320 --> 04:31.490
You know, they say love changes a maiden.

04:31.490 --> 04:33.200
Huh?! Don't tell me that...

04:33.980 --> 04:35.140
What are you saying?

04:35.140 --> 04:36.210
Stop it, please.

04:36.210 --> 04:38.470
Well, it's only natural.

04:38.470 --> 04:42.210
I mean, Tsubasa is really cool!

04:42.210 --> 04:44.540
Tch! It's all about Tsubasa, eh?

04:44.540 --> 04:46.630
We're also members of Nankatsu Middle School.

04:47.380 --> 04:51.220
Hah! I'd love to see the weirdo that falls in love with you, Ishizaki.

04:51.220 --> 04:52.310
What did you say?!

04:52.310 --> 04:53.940
Say it again, I dare you!

04:53.940 --> 04:55.530
Like I'd get scared!

04:57.060 --> 05:01.580
The regional preliminaries for the summer
tournament are about to start, aren't they?

05:01.580 --> 05:03.140
How are you feeling about them?

05:03.140 --> 05:08.070
We'll do our best in every match, just as we've done every year!

05:08.070 --> 05:13.660
It seems as though this year, your rivals are quite enthusiastic about overthrowing the reigning champions!

05:13.660 --> 05:18.270
On Toho Academy, Kojiro Hyuga's partner from elementary school,

05:18.270 --> 05:21.540
Takeshi Sawada, has finally joined the squad.

05:21.540 --> 05:23.440
As for Hokkaido's Furano Middle School,

05:23.440 --> 05:27.800
they are honing their teamwork even more, with their captain, Matsuyama, at the core.

05:27.800 --> 05:30.070
Hanawa Middle School, with the Tachibana Twins,

05:30.070 --> 05:33.350
and Musashi Middle School, with Misugi, the Ace of Glass,

05:33.350 --> 05:37.110
are also rumored to be planning to overthrow Nankatsu Middle School this year.

05:37.110 --> 05:38.600
I couldn't ask for more.

05:38.600 --> 05:40.860
I don't plan losing, that's for sure.

05:40.860 --> 05:42.560
Thank you very much for your time.

05:42.560 --> 05:45.150
We expect a good fight from you in the tournament.

05:45.150 --> 05:46.140
See you then!

05:46.140 --> 05:47.720
Thank you!

05:48.920 --> 05:49.860
<i>Right.</i>

05:50.460 --> 05:53.630
<i>Hyuga, Misugi and the rest...</i>

05:53.630 --> 05:55.250
<i>They're all trying their best.</i>

05:57.720 --> 06:01.730
<i>But Misaki... How are you doing now, I wonder?</i>

06:01.730 --> 06:04.750
<i>It's hard to believe you haven't kept in touch since then.</i>

06:05.490 --> 06:08.840
<i>And Roberto, too...</i>

06:13.630 --> 06:18.810
<i>After you left, I changed from forward
to midfielder, just as you told me to.</i>

06:18.810 --> 06:22.270
<i>I believed in and followed the directions
in the notebook you left for me.</i>

06:22.270 --> 06:27.440
<i>I learned new moves, and built up my stamina accordingly.</i>

06:27.440 --> 06:32.480
<i>I dedicated myself to absorbing these techniques,
your approach to the game,</i>

06:32.480 --> 06:34.700
<i>and it just makes me admire Brazil even more.</i>

06:35.430 --> 06:40.250
<i>My dream about the country of football,
Brazil, grows larger each day.</i>

06:42.250 --> 06:48.220
<i>Queria falar mais devagar que disse? Manda vir um taxi.</i>

06:45.840 --> 06:49.130
Sign: Tsubasa's Portuguese Home Tutor Carlos

06:48.220 --> 06:49.480
<i>Pronto!</i>

06:49.480 --> 06:52.340
Tsubasa, your pronunciation's gotten really good!

06:52.340 --> 06:53.700
Seriously?

06:54.350 --> 06:56.160
Where are you going, Carlos?

06:56.160 --> 06:58.600
Just a quick restroom break!

06:58.600 --> 07:00.850
"<i>Retrete</i>," right?

07:02.160 --> 07:03.650
Hey, Carlos.

07:03.650 --> 07:07.320
How is Tsubasa's Portuguese doing?

07:07.320 --> 07:11.990
As far as I've seen, he won't have any issues being conversational.

07:11.990 --> 07:13.720
He is all good!

07:13.720 --> 07:15.260
No need to worry.

07:15.260 --> 07:18.200
But ma'am, sir, are you going to be okay?

07:18.200 --> 07:19.380
Huh?

07:19.380 --> 07:22.720
Do you really intend to let Tsubasa go to Brazil?

07:22.720 --> 07:24.930
He is your one and only precious son.

07:26.160 --> 07:28.210
We've already steeled our resolve.

07:28.210 --> 07:33.230
People from the National Football Federation are helping us, as well.

07:33.230 --> 07:37.300
As soon as he graduates from middle school,
we will be sending him over.

07:38.040 --> 07:45.860
But before that, Tsubasa, make sure you spend your last summer in Japan well, so you can leave with no regrets.

07:45.860 --> 07:48.230
Sign: Certain V3 Tournament Victory!

07:50.320 --> 07:52.440
They've finally announced them.

07:52.440 --> 07:55.740
These are the brackets for the prefectural preliminaries!

07:57.030 --> 08:01.160
Since we're seeded, we won't play until the second round, right?

08:01.160 --> 08:03.340
You know, the results won't change even if you check.

08:03.340 --> 08:06.790
It's not like there's a team in the area that can beat us.

08:06.790 --> 08:10.630
Sir, Otomo Middle School is seeded on the other side, no?

08:10.630 --> 08:13.300
Yeah, we can only play them in the finals match.

08:13.300 --> 08:18.680
Otomo is the team Kishida, Urabe, Nakayama and Nishio are in, right?

08:18.680 --> 08:21.640
Rumor has it they received a big boost this year, too.

08:21.640 --> 08:23.780
What are you so scared of?

08:23.780 --> 08:25.630
I mean, if you're so worried about them,

08:25.630 --> 08:28.580
let's just set up a practice match and kick them around!

08:28.580 --> 08:31.720
That very same team already refused a practice match with us.

08:31.720 --> 08:32.490
Huh?

08:32.490 --> 08:36.030
So, in other words, they don't want to show their hand, yet.

08:36.030 --> 08:37.110
Exactly.

08:37.110 --> 08:41.550
Goes to show how passionate they are about defeating Nankatsu, this year.

08:41.550 --> 08:43.670
No matter the opponent, all we need to do is win.

08:43.670 --> 08:46.310
Let's focus on the prefectural tournament!

08:46.310 --> 08:47.330
Yeah!

08:47.330 --> 08:51.250
NANKATSU MUNICIPALITY - NANKATSU MIDDLE SCHOOL

08:54.260 --> 08:55.400
All right! Get on them!

08:55.400 --> 08:56.830
Score another one!

08:57.470 --> 09:00.640
Isn't that Urabe with his group watching from over there?

09:01.080 --> 09:02.790
Yes, looks like it's Otomo Middle School.

09:02.790 --> 09:04.640
It looks like they're here to scout.

09:04.640 --> 09:06.250
It's headed your way, Ishizaki!

09:06.250 --> 09:07.440
Clearing it!

09:08.160 --> 09:08.940
The match is over!

09:12.860 --> 09:15.440
Hey! It's been a long time, guys!

09:15.440 --> 09:17.440
Could you do me a favor and get the ball?

09:17.440 --> 09:19.440
Get here and take it if you want.

09:19.440 --> 09:20.950
What?!

09:20.950 --> 09:22.780
We are enemies now.

09:22.780 --> 09:24.620
You're acting awfully familiar.

09:24.620 --> 09:25.940
What did you say?!

09:25.940 --> 09:30.450
Don't act so tough, when all you've done is turn down our requests for practice matches!

09:30.450 --> 09:32.500
How dare you walk around, spouting such nonsense?

09:32.500 --> 09:35.330
We're not really hiding from you guys.

09:35.330 --> 09:40.380
It just wouldn't be fun to put an end to Nankatsu's winning streak in a practice match.

09:40.380 --> 09:43.510
If we're gonna do that, we'd rather it be at the prefectural tournament finals, that's all!

09:44.660 --> 09:45.930
Now, now!

09:45.930 --> 09:50.530
You're both former teammates.

09:50.530 --> 09:52.440
There's no need to get all worked up.

09:52.440 --> 09:55.440
Let us show you our strength!

09:57.240 --> 09:59.200
Tsubasa, the ball's headed your way!

10:01.490 --> 10:03.010
Let's go!

10:03.010 --> 10:05.010
whats this, gaara vs lee? one of the best shounen fights eva

10:10.740 --> 10:11.750
Those movements...

10:11.750 --> 10:14.300
It's like a school of sharks aiming for their prey!

10:14.300 --> 10:16.050
Who are those guys?

10:16.050 --> 10:20.840
Urabe, Kishida, Nishio and even Nakayama...

10:20.840 --> 10:23.920
Coach, is it all right for us to not stop them?

10:25.710 --> 10:27.730
Hey, what's wrong, Tsubasa?

10:30.550 --> 10:32.440
They stole the ball from Tsubasa!

10:32.440 --> 10:33.370
Impossible!

10:33.370 --> 10:34.570
It was four on one,

10:34.570 --> 10:35.930
but they took it from Tsubasa!

10:35.930 --> 10:36.320
Nitta!

10:37.280 --> 10:38.030
Yes!

10:39.160 --> 10:39.860
<i>He is fast.</i>

10:39.860 --> 10:41.530
<i>He's unrefined, but that player is...</i>

10:41.980 --> 10:42.780
Morisaki!

10:45.110 --> 10:48.080
Go for it, my Falcon Shot!

10:54.310 --> 10:56.090
What?!

10:58.580 --> 11:02.740
Had a taste of it Nankatsu?
This is our strength!

11:02.740 --> 11:04.140
What did you say?!

11:04.140 --> 11:06.010
That's right!

11:06.010 --> 11:10.140
We, Otomo Middle School, will be the ones
participating in the national tournament!

11:14.070 --> 11:17.230
Tsubasa, don't be disheartened.

11:17.230 --> 11:23.100
They were part of the Nankatsu SC that
became national champions, after all.

11:23.100 --> 11:24.020
Yeah.

11:24.020 --> 11:26.740
They've improved a considerable amount, though.

11:26.740 --> 11:30.290
We can't let our guard down, even in the preliminaries.

11:27.520 --> 11:31.160
<i>Their speed was nothing like it used to be, that's for sure.</i>

11:30.290 --> 11:33.220
It's impossible for us to lose, though.

11:31.160 --> 11:34.500
<i>But their speed wasn't the only reason I lost the ball...</i>

11:34.970 --> 11:36.500
<i>That ball he kicked...</i>

11:36.500 --> 11:40.420
<i>When I trapped that, my leg was numb afterwards.</i>

11:41.030 --> 11:43.760
<i>That hasn't happened since that match...</i>

11:45.730 --> 11:47.800
<i>They said his name was Nitta, right?</i>

11:47.800 --> 11:49.690
<i>Who is he exactly?</i>

11:58.120 --> 11:59.530
Shun Nitta.

11:59.530 --> 12:03.700
Well, I could refer to him as the savior of Nankatsu SC.

12:04.220 --> 12:05.450
Savior?

12:05.450 --> 12:06.800
That's right.

12:06.800 --> 12:11.120
Nitta is fast enough to run 100 meters in 11 seconds.

12:11.120 --> 12:13.900
Also, his legs are incredibly flexible.

12:13.900 --> 12:16.860
His special move, his so-called Falcon Shot,

12:16.860 --> 12:19.110
is a result of that flexibility.

12:19.110 --> 12:21.160
The sharpness of it is top-notch.

12:21.160 --> 12:23.220
I see, I was surprised when I saw it, too.

12:23.220 --> 12:26.800
Also, they say he plays with a lot of guts.

12:26.800 --> 12:31.710
He completely defeated Meiwa FC's Takeshi Sawada, despite Sawada being his senior,

12:31.710 --> 12:37.230
and he carried Nankatsu SC to the championship after you and your classmates graduated from the team.

12:37.230 --> 12:42.250
Truth be told, it won't be easy to participate in the Nationals this year.

12:42.250 --> 12:43.120
Right.

12:43.120 --> 12:45.610
Excuse me, you are Tsubasa Ozora, right?

12:45.610 --> 12:47.820
Would you please watch our practice?

12:47.820 --> 12:51.790
We want to be able to shoot like you, Tsubasa.

12:51.790 --> 12:53.950
Of course, I'd love to!

12:53.950 --> 12:56.000
Otomo... Fight!

12:56.000 --> 12:56.480
Yeah!

12:56.480 --> 12:56.840
Fight!

12:56.840 --> 12:57.280
Yeah!

12:57.280 --> 12:57.640
Fight!

12:57.640 --> 12:58.130
Yeah!

12:58.130 --> 12:58.480
Fight!

12:58.480 --> 12:59.260
Yeah!

12:59.260 --> 13:01.050
Hey Urabe, look at that.

13:01.050 --> 13:01.750
What?

13:01.750 --> 13:02.800
Here it goes!

13:06.390 --> 13:08.050
Tsubasa!

13:08.700 --> 13:09.640
Urabe!

13:09.640 --> 13:12.130
The tournament is just around the corner.

13:12.130 --> 13:14.640
Are you sure you have time to play around with kids?

13:14.640 --> 13:18.000
We showed you how strong we were yesterday,

13:18.000 --> 13:20.060
yet you seem completely unconcerned!

13:20.650 --> 13:22.060
Just watch us, Tsubasa!

13:22.060 --> 13:27.570
We'll make you get off your high horse in the prefectural tournament!

13:27.570 --> 13:29.780
Urabe, you're going too far.

13:29.780 --> 13:31.450
All right, let's go.

13:31.450 --> 13:32.200
Yes!

13:35.330 --> 13:37.920
I can already see how this will end.

13:37.920 --> 13:42.440
But please stay at least until the finals, Tsubasa.

13:44.780 --> 13:50.220
They've been passing by this pitch daily for two years, now.

13:50.220 --> 13:50.890
What?

13:50.890 --> 13:54.390
Coming here from Otomo Middle School and back is roughly 30km.

13:54.390 --> 13:57.890
That's not a distance you can run with your usual drive.

13:57.890 --> 14:01.800
Otomo Middle School's defense is among the best in the prefecture.

14:01.800 --> 14:04.420
But, they were just missing some offense.

14:04.420 --> 14:07.650
With Nitta joining this year, they finally have a trump card.

14:07.650 --> 14:12.830
The final piece is in place, and that is now complete.

14:11.570 --> 14:12.830
SIGN: OTOMO MIDDLE SCHOOL

14:20.620 --> 14:23.170
I'll count on you tomorrow too, friend!

14:28.200 --> 14:29.300
<i>That's right.</i>

14:29.300 --> 14:31.680
<i>We've let our guard down along the way.</i>

14:31.680 --> 14:35.260
<i>We've started to think that we'll always win.</i>

14:35.260 --> 14:37.850
<i>We've been too vain!</i>

14:37.850 --> 14:43.860
<i>The only way to overcome that kind of conceit is to practice!</i>

14:43.860 --> 14:47.110
<i>We must strengthen ourselves, and get our confidence back!</i>

14:47.110 --> 14:50.860
<i>There's no other way!</i>

14:56.440 --> 14:57.870
Here's a towel for you.

14:57.870 --> 14:59.370
Manager!

14:59.370 --> 15:01.510
Wipe off your sweat.

15:01.510 --> 15:03.540
Then you can practice some more.

15:04.880 --> 15:06.380
All right, here I go!

15:09.280 --> 15:12.300
Next, we'll split in two groups and have a mini-match, 5 against 4!

15:12.950 --> 15:15.620
Hey, Tsubasa. I think you're going too fast.

15:15.620 --> 15:18.310
He's right. Let's take a little break.

15:18.310 --> 15:20.020
Did you not hear me?

15:20.020 --> 15:21.310
5 against 4!

15:21.750 --> 15:24.680
We'll have to play under the summer sun

15:24.680 --> 15:28.110
during the prefectural tournament and then the Nationals.

15:28.110 --> 15:31.050
Winning a third time with that mindset is impossible.

15:31.050 --> 15:35.620
You say that, but think about us and our underclassmen a little.

15:35.620 --> 15:37.620
So guys, it's 5 against 4!

15:37.620 --> 15:39.620
What the hell, Tsubasa?!

15:39.620 --> 15:41.120
Stop it, you two!

15:42.320 --> 15:43.560
Coach...

15:43.560 --> 15:48.610
After a 5 minute break, the 3rd year regulars will play against the first and the second years.

15:48.610 --> 15:51.440
Tsubasa, you'll play in the latter team.

15:51.440 --> 15:52.130
Wha—

15:52.130 --> 15:53.680
Is that all right, Tsubasa?

15:53.680 --> 15:55.090
Yes!

15:56.120 --> 15:59.510
Don't you think Tsubasa's a little bit too nervous?

15:59.510 --> 16:00.680
Agreed.

16:00.680 --> 16:03.930
We're trying to do our best here, too.

16:03.930 --> 16:05.150
Is that really so?

16:06.060 --> 16:07.540
What do you mean?

16:07.540 --> 16:08.650
Nothing really.

16:08.650 --> 16:11.650
I just thought that your eyes looked different.

16:13.180 --> 16:16.990
Tsubasa's eyes and yours just look different to me.

16:16.990 --> 16:18.990
Tsubasa!

16:21.980 --> 16:25.790
- Guys, don't panic and take your time.
- Okay!

16:23.000 --> 16:25.790
Damn it. What does she mean by, "eyes looked different"?

16:25.790 --> 16:29.290
Let's show them we can play well enough even without Tsubasa!

16:29.290 --> 16:30.170
Yeah!

16:31.210 --> 16:32.840
Let's go, Tsubasa!

16:32.840 --> 16:33.640
Stop him!

16:33.640 --> 16:34.420
Okay!

16:35.300 --> 16:36.220
Don't get so cocky!

16:40.470 --> 16:44.520
Izawa, your ball keeping is still half-baked!

16:44.520 --> 16:45.440
Here!

16:46.190 --> 16:48.020
Y-yes!

16:48.020 --> 16:49.560
Got it!

16:49.560 --> 16:50.820
Taki, go!

16:51.690 --> 16:54.310
All right, I'll dribble next to the line.

16:54.310 --> 16:54.950
Taki!

16:55.890 --> 16:58.030
You rely too much on your special move!

16:58.740 --> 17:00.990
Think of other attack patterns!

17:00.990 --> 17:01.740
Taki!

17:01.740 --> 17:04.160
Kisugi! Look around you!

17:05.560 --> 17:07.840
How is it that you're being marked this easily?

17:07.840 --> 17:12.140
If you're going to receive a cross,
you should move more and create some space!

17:12.140 --> 17:13.170
Tsubasa...

17:14.130 --> 17:16.180
Here we go! Follow my lead!

17:16.180 --> 17:16.930
Yeah!

17:16.930 --> 17:18.410
We'll stop him, Takasugi!

17:18.410 --> 17:18.930
Okay!

17:20.670 --> 17:21.310
You bastard!

17:23.140 --> 17:27.140
Did you think this would be enough to protect Nankatsu's goal?

17:32.730 --> 17:34.170
Morisaki, too!

17:34.170 --> 17:37.870
Wakabayashi would have stopped such a shot lightly with his chest!

17:40.760 --> 17:42.530
Tsubasa!

17:50.000 --> 17:51.540
All right, let's do this!

17:51.540 --> 17:52.880
It begins now!

17:52.880 --> 17:54.440
Come at us once more, Tsubasa!

17:54.440 --> 17:57.550
Yeah! I won't let you steal the ball easily this time!

17:57.550 --> 17:59.280
We'll stop you this time!

17:59.280 --> 18:00.260
Guys...

18:01.260 --> 18:03.890
Just what the hell is going on?

18:03.890 --> 18:04.880
Let's do this!

18:04.880 --> 18:05.390
Yeah!

18:05.390 --> 18:07.140
That's right!

18:07.140 --> 18:09.740
Well, a healthy dose of rivalry makes them strong.

18:09.740 --> 18:10.400
Yes.

18:10.400 --> 18:14.690
Everyone's eyes have started to have the same sparkle as Tsubasa's.

18:14.690 --> 18:17.090
<i>Seeing through that...</i>

18:17.090 --> 18:20.700
<i>I can't hold a candle against Sanae.</i>

18:30.340 --> 18:31.630
Are you all right?

18:31.630 --> 18:34.280
You really are huge.

18:34.280 --> 18:37.630
Yeah. Your friend is good at this.

18:37.630 --> 18:38.820
Didn't I tell you so?

18:38.820 --> 18:43.140
Ichijo is the goalkeeper from when I became the champion at Nankatsu.

18:43.740 --> 18:44.890
I see...

18:44.890 --> 18:48.100
You became champion while you attacked and he protected the goal.

18:49.140 --> 18:50.160
All right!

18:50.160 --> 18:53.700
With this, we are one step closer to perfecting Otomo's play.

18:53.700 --> 18:56.110
This year, we'll definitely overthrow Nankatsu!

18:58.870 --> 19:02.260
<i>Today marks the beginning of the Shizuoka Prefectural Tournament</i>

19:02.260 --> 19:05.740
<i>before the National Middle School Football Tournament.</i>

19:05.740 --> 19:07.590
So, it begins again.

19:07.590 --> 19:08.480
Yeah.

19:10.000 --> 19:11.500
Genzo Wakabayashi - Mail

19:12.060 --> 19:13.080
Wakabayashi!

19:14.720 --> 19:15.710
Hey, wait.

19:15.710 --> 19:18.860
"Tsubasa and everyone from Nankatsu Middle School.

19:18.860 --> 19:21.720
The preliminaries must be about to start in Japan.

19:21.720 --> 19:24.740
Good luck with getting your third victory in the Nationals.

19:24.740 --> 19:26.940
I'll be cheering from afar in Germany.

19:26.940 --> 19:29.440
Former goalkeeper of Nankatsu SC,

19:29.440 --> 19:31.230
Genzo Wakabayashi"

19:31.230 --> 19:34.690
Wakabayashi hasn't forgotten about us.

19:36.660 --> 19:37.980
Tsubasa!

19:38.420 --> 19:39.790
Mr. Katagiri!

19:39.790 --> 19:41.150
It's been a while.

19:41.150 --> 19:44.740
SIGN: JAPANESE FOOTBALL FEDERATION - MUNEMASA KATAGIRI

19:41.150 --> 19:44.740
I haven't seen you since the high school training camp in spring, right?

19:45.940 --> 19:50.650
I sent many of your videos to the football clubs in Brazil.

19:50.650 --> 19:54.160
As I thought, they were quite interested in your skills.

19:54.160 --> 19:57.720
So after I graduate, I can immediately go to Brazil, right?

19:57.720 --> 19:58.250
Yes.

19:58.250 --> 20:00.380
But we're dealing with the pros here.

20:00.380 --> 20:02.170
Unless they see you play themselves,

20:02.170 --> 20:04.760
they won't be signing a contract with you right away.

20:04.760 --> 20:05.390
I know.

20:05.390 --> 20:08.640
For now, just focus on giving your all in this tournament.

20:08.640 --> 20:10.640
We'll talk about Brazil after that.

20:11.280 --> 20:13.640
Make sure you win, Tsubasa.

20:14.720 --> 20:17.940
First, you'll create a legend here in Japan.

20:17.940 --> 20:19.860
Winning the title 3 years in a row...

20:19.860 --> 20:24.200
Well, if you add your elementary school title in there too, that'd make it 4 times.

20:23.700 --> 20:29.490
SIGN: SHIZUOKA PREFECTURE JUNIOR HIGH FOOTBALL TOURNAMENT - CHAMPION

20:24.200 --> 20:26.700
It's been 4 years since you moved to Nankatsu.

20:26.700 --> 20:29.490
You'll be going to Brazil undefeated.

20:29.490 --> 20:32.280
Then, you should stand at the top in Brazil, too.

20:32.280 --> 20:37.970
When you become #1 in that country, Japan's football will change!

20:37.970 --> 20:42.760
Tsubasa, you'll lead the way and change this country's football!

20:42.760 --> 20:44.010
Yes!

20:44.940 --> 20:48.010
I'll definitely win a third consecutive championship.

20:48.530 --> 20:50.510
We won't lose to anyone!

20:53.700 --> 20:56.320
<i>That's right, I almost forgot about that...</i>

20:58.520 --> 21:02.530
<i>This will be the last year I'll be spending with Tsubasa.</i>

21:04.260 --> 21:06.530
<i>It finally starts!</i>

21:06.530 --> 21:09.490
<i>It's time for the Shizuoka Prefectural Football Tournament!</i>

21:09.490 --> 21:11.740
<i>The championship pennant is being returned.</i>

21:11.740 --> 21:17.000
<i>Last year's champion was Nankatsu Middle School, led by their captain Tsubasa.</i>

21:17.000 --> 21:20.750
<i>Ever since he started school there, they haven't known defeat,</i>

21:20.750 --> 21:23.840
<i>and have been the holder of the champion's title, 2 years running.</i>

21:23.840 --> 21:28.640
Ishizaki! We'll be getting that championship pennant this year.

21:28.640 --> 21:30.790
What the hell are you saying?

21:30.790 --> 21:33.970
You should talk after you get to the finals.

21:33.970 --> 21:39.850
We'll definitely reach the finals while scoring more goals than you.

21:39.850 --> 21:41.310
You must be joking!

21:41.310 --> 21:42.940
We won't lose.

21:42.940 --> 21:44.610
All right then, let's bet on it!

21:44.610 --> 21:47.740
We'll have a contest about who scores more goals until the finals.

21:47.740 --> 21:50.950
The loser will have to do anything the winner says.

21:50.950 --> 21:52.990
Now we're talking!

21:52.990 --> 21:54.740
I accept your challenge!

21:54.740 --> 21:55.500
Urabe!

21:55.500 --> 21:56.710
Ishizaki!

21:57.980 --> 22:00.590
<i>Keep winning until the finals.</i>

22:00.590 --> 22:03.440
<i>I'll definitely defeat you there.</i>

22:04.630 --> 22:05.460
What!

22:07.900 --> 22:10.300
<i>So you think you have the luxury to smile, huh?</i>

22:10.900 --> 22:16.470
<i>I'll make sure that your face is wracked with panic and the feeling of defeat in the finals!</i>

22:16.470 --> 22:20.060
<i>Just watch me, Tsubasa Ozora!</i>

22:38.790 --> 22:44.840
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.790 --> 22:44.840
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.840 --> 22:50.840
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.840 --> 22:50.840
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.840 --> 22:56.890
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.840 --> 22:56.890
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.890 --> 23:01.520
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.890 --> 23:01.520
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.150 --> 23:07.810
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.150 --> 23:07.810
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.150 --> 23:15.240
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.150 --> 23:15.240
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.240 --> 23:21.290
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.290 --> 23:25.750
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.290 --> 23:25.750
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.050 --> 23:33.380
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.050 --> 23:33.380
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.380 --> 23:39.430
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.430 --> 23:45.730
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.430 --> 23:45.730
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:50.070 --> 24:00.720
COMING UP, EPISODE 30:
PREFECTURAL TOURNAMENT FINALS!
FALCON SHOT APPEARS!
